{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>הלהן תשברנה</b>. The nun [is] in place of the mem, and [it is] the opposite of 'כי מר לי מאד מכם'. And they came [to] Bethlehem; the word תשברנה is joined with the letter lamed or with the word אל, like 'עיני כל אליך ישברו'." "<b>תעגנה</b>. From the nifal binyan, and it has no cognate." "<b>לבלתי היות לאיש</b>. That each of them be to a man, like 'ויתלו שניהם על עץ'." "<b>אל בנותי</b>. That is, do not go with me." "<b>כי יצאה בי</b>. The decree of HaShem that went out from before Him, or that she was delivered and it went out in me until it was seen." "<b>יד ה'</b>. A blow, for 'by hand' it is in human language [that] the matter is written." "<b>שבה יבמתך</b>. From the root of יבמה, we have already explained it in the Torah." "<b>אל עמה ואל אלהיה</b>. Until [the point] that they converted."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:21.870332347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}